        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(dreaming): drop heartbeat assistant responses from dream corpus",
        "body": "Fixes #103720\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nDreaming Light and REM phases produce ghost entries (\"A memory trace surfaced, but details were unavailable in this run.\") instead of real dream content. The dreaming ingestion pipeline filters heartbeat user messages (containing `[OpenClaw heartbeat poll]`) via `sanitizeSessionText`, but the paired assistant response is only dropped when it is the exact string `HEARTBEAT_OK`. Local models frequently respond with natural-language acknowledgments (e.g. \"Heartbeat received. Main is active.\") which pass through the sanitizer unchanged and enter the dream corpus as low-confidence (0.58) memory snippets.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`sanitizeSessionText` in `session-files.ts` filters heartbeat user messages via `isGeneratedHeartbeatPromptMessage` (checks for `[OpenClaw heartbeat poll]`), but the assistant-side filter is only:\n```js\nif (role === \"assistant\" && normalized === HEARTBEAT_TOKEN) {\n  return null;\n}\n```\nThis exact-string match misses natural-language acknowledgments. The existing `isHeartbeatOkResponse` helper in `heartbeat.ts` also relies on token presence, so importing it wouldn't help either.\n\nThe code deliberately avoids cross-message coupling for `[cron:...]` and `System (untrusted): ...` patterns because those are user-spoofable (see PR #70737). The heartbeat prompt pattern is injected by the runtime and cannot be spoofed, making this a safe exception.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Dreaming Light and REM phases produce real dream content instead of ghost entries\n- 12 ghost entries in our main agent DREAMS.md across June 24–July 4\n- 7 ghost entries in our secondary agent (elfo) DREAMS.md across June 28–July 4\n- Pattern matches the issue description exactly: \"A memory trace surfaced, but details were unavailable in this run.\"\n- No change to memory_search (shared corpus lister untouched)\n- No change to archive/deleted transcript handling (already correct in dreaming-phases.ts)\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `oxlint`: 0 warnings / 0 errors\n- 39 tests pass (38 existing + 1 new heartbeat-specific test)\n- Change is 27 insertions, 7 deletions in one function\n- Heartbeat prompt pattern is runtime-injected, not user-spoofable — safe exception to cross-message coupling rule\n- Flag clears harmlessly on back-to-back user messages (no dangling state)\n\n```bash\n$ npx oxlint packages/memory-host-sdk/src/host/session-files.ts\nFound 0 warnings and 0 errors.\n\n$ npx vitest run packages/memory-host-sdk/src/host/session-files.test.ts\n ✓ 39 tests passed (39)\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n Duration  2.67s\n```\n\n## Risk checklist\n\nmerge-risk: Low\n\n- [x] Low risk declaration: additive flag tracking in one function, only triggers on runtime-injected heartbeat prompts\n- [x] 27 insertions, 7 deletions — well within the Diamond Lobster 100-line limit\n- [x] No change to archive/deleted transcript handling (already correct in dreaming-phases.ts)\n- [x] No change to memory_search (shared corpus lister untouched)\n- [x] Heartbeat prompt pattern is non-spoofable — safe exception to cross-message coupling rule\n- [x] Flag clears harmlessly on back-to-back user messages (no dangling state)\n- [x] New test verifies heartbeat user + natural-language assistant response are both dropped",
        "branch": "fix/dreaming-heartbeat-filter",
        "head_sha": "baa673c41941e699c871d31503bb620d507ec4fd",
